WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.468
Let's go to the courthouse.

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.836
CNN's senior crime

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.037
and justice correspondent

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.071
Shimon Prokupecz

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:05.872
and senior

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:06.539
legal affairs

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.675
correspondent Paula Reid are both there.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.443
Paula, I want to start with you

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.645
because several media outlets,

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.214
including CNN, petitioned

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:14.748
the judge

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.716
to unseal the document early

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.285
and also allow cameras in the courtroom

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.186
What can you tell us

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.322
about the status of that supporters,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.190
Congressman?

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.191
That's right, Dan.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:25.992
There has been this push

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.460
for more transparency

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.429
from media organizations

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.897
We wanted the indictment

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:31.598
to be unsealed

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.199
ahead of tomorrow's arraignment

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.768
when it is historically

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.969
usually revealed for the force

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:36.803
first time.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:37.137
And also,

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.571
there's been a push for cameras

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.572
in the courtroom

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.540
arguing that, yes,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.941
while there are not usually cameras

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.243
in Manhattan courtrooms,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.478
that there is no greater public interest

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:46.780
than when you are talking

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.680
about the arraignment

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.782
of a former president

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.150
of the United States.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.918
Now, the judge gave both the prosecutors

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.353
and the defense at 1 p.m.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.687
today to weigh in.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.522
And the prosecutors

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.756
took no stance on this.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.891
But surprisingly,

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:58.324
the former

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:58.825
president's

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.927
legal team is opposing cameras

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.895
in the courtroom.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.996
Now, they are really leaning

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:03.763
into the idea

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.865
that this is a security risk.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:06.299
They're saying

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.767
that this could potentially contribute

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.234
to a court

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.503
circus like atmosphere in the courtroom.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.738
And they're also saying

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.173
that having cameras in the courtroom

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.075
would go against the former president's

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.043
right to a presumption of innocence.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:17.410
But, Dana,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:17.911
this is somewhat

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.112
surprising for someone

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:19.679
who is, of course,

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.815
a very successful reality star.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:22.615
But look, this judge

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.284
historically has not been in favor

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.318
of having cameras

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.886
even in high profile cases.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.822
So now that the defense has come out

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:29.823
against that,

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.157
it's looking less likely

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.326
that we will get this this access.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:33.726
Yeah.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.761
I mean, in some ways it's

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.795
surprising in other ways,

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.896
since he is a candidate

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.632
to be president again, not as surprising.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.969
The images of the motorcade going to to

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.805
to his plane and his plane taking off.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.140
Those are the images I believe

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.374
we're going to see in a Trump

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.576
ad if there's going to be one.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.410
He doesn't necessarily

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.078
want one in the courtroom.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.012
Speaking of the courtroom,

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.081
what can you tell us about the changes

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.483
to Trump's legal team?

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.654
Well, now that indictment has been filed,

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.755
even though it's under seal,

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.491
the former president has added

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.459
an attorney to his legal team.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.660
This is not unusual

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.261
particularly in these

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.462
ongoing investigations.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.363
We see people coming

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.631
and going from the team.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.533
In this case, his attorney, Todd Blanch,

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.568
he has been added to the defense team,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.202
but a lot of people

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.670
speculating about what that means

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.037
for Joe

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.372
Tacopina, who has really been

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.573
the most forward facing

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.108
member of the defense team.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.843
I spoke to Joe a short time ago, though.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.278
He said he's still on the team

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.480
and he says he will be the lead counsel

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.649
during the hearing tomorrow.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.551
And someone I want to turn to you.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:32.852
There's been a lot of concern,

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:33.920
a lot of speculation,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.954
a lot of trepidation

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:35.688
related to

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.123
what could be coming

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.625
from a security perspective.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.093
What's your sense of things right now

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:40.460
in terms

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.629
from what the NYPD is prepared to do,

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.663
both today, tomorrow,

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.664
kind of the whole assessment

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.398
of things going forward

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.403
Well, certainly securing the

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.171
former president,

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.505
making sure he gets inside

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.806
the building here

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.474
behind us,

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.442
that's going to be the number one

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.977
priority getting him in there,

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:58.845
making sure

00:02:58.845 --> 00:02:59.479
no one tries

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.114
to interrupt the proceedings.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.081
But the issue now is

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.384
if they're not going to have Phil cameras

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.118
in the courtroom,

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:05.919
every image

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.121
that we could possibly get of the former

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.290
president is going to be important.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.891
And one of those images

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.127
could come here on Hogan Place.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:14.761
This is where

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.930
the district attorney's office is

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.965
This is where we expect the motorcade

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.734
with the former president to drive down.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.770
We expect that he's going to

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.672
come out of the car

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.373
and then walk through the doors

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:30.076
of one polling place, which is here

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.746
to my right, and walk in and surrender

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.648
to the district attorney's office

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.883
and then essentially

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.252
he will be under arrest.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.353
And at that point is

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.721
when the arrest, processing,

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.256
the fingerprinting

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.991
or the paperwork that comes along with

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.426
that will take place

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.528
but he will walk into these doors.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.562
He will be met there

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.731
by district attorney staff,

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:54.334
the investigators on the case.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.169
Those are the people that will be making

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:56.703
the arrest.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.071
And then they will take him upstairs

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.239
where they will do the processing.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.406
But right now,

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:01.774
as they prepare for tomorrow,

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.543
we're seeing a lot of barricades

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.043
here today.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.411
Certainly we're seeing

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.546
several more

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:10.149
officers, court officers, NYPD personnel.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.251
And tomorrow,

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.319
what we expect is that this entire street

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.355
is going to be closed off

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.557
as they bring the motorcade through here.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.992
But then also the streets

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.727
surrounding the courthouse

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.728
because there is

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.429
some concern for protesters

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.833
and there's
a lot of choreography going here,

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.534
going on right now.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.469
Certainly a lot to watch

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.303
tomorrow as well.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.471
And Shimon

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:31.871
is going to be there

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.539
for all of it from Professor Paul Read.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.173
Thanks so much.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.075
I want to get back out to Katelyn

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.110
outside Trump Tower,

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.478
and I'd like her opinion

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.146
on whether it's a regular thing

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:40.847
for the president

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:41.614
to be against

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.950
creating a circus like atmosphere

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.885
from a media perspective.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.654
Kevin, you have any thoughts on that?

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:51.591
Yeah,

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.892
there'll be some questions about that.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.060
Of course, that is coming from the Trump

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:54.827
legal team.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:55.461
We should know

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.030
we are here outside of Trump Tower,

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.332
just blocks away from where Shimon is.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:04:59.699
We have seen

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:00.700
its chief national affairs

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.335
correspondent Jeff Zeleny, and CNN

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.736
senior legal analyst, silicone

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.937
and both with us.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:05.605
Eliot,

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.840
the idea that they don't want cameras

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.608
to be in the courtroom,

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.543
you know this off in this courthouse

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:11.210
very well.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.545
Are you surprised by that?

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.447
No, not I think that's what I expected.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.683
So ordinarily in New York state courts

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.350
and that's what we are

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.184
we're not in federal court.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.185
We're in state court.

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.020
The rule is no cameras in the courtroom.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.289
However, the judge does have discretion.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.757
The judge can say, I'm

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:25.758
going to allow them.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:26.626
And what the judge has to

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.294
balance is on the one hand,

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.329
the need for transparency

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:30.063
in the public interest,

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.831
which is not just high here,

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.800
but I would say unprecedented in terms

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.001
of how high it is.

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:35.868
On the other hand,

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.071
the need to protect the presumption

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.439
of innocence of the defendant

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:41.240
and the thinking there as well.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.275
The image of somebody

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.743
standing at a defendant's table,

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.944
even if not in handcuffs,

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:46.546
even if not in prison garb,

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:49.048
still could be influential on our jury.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.049
And let's remember,

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.417
our whole jury pool is watching.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.553
So I think it's not at all surprising

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.188
that the defense does not want cameras

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:55.788
in there.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.123
I mean,
an image of a person

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.057
standing at a defense table

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.192
could be even more prejudicial

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.660
than a mug shot, if you think about it.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.794
So we will see.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:02.762
What the judge decides on

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:04.564
this is important to keep in mind.

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.366
Tomorrow's arraignment is going to last

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.800
no more than 10 minutes.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.635
Maybe as short as 5 minutes.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.470
So the judge will make

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.904
his decision on tomorrow.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:12.472
Ultimately, it's

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:14.173
going to be a much bigger question about

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.541
does the judge allow cameras in

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.310
for the trial if there is a trial. Right.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.077
And what does this judge

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:18.811
have a history of doing

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:19.645
when it comes to camera?

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:20.813
Yes.
So this judge historically

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.715
has not been open to the idea of cameras.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:23.850
He denied a request

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:24.917
to have cameras in the Trump

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:25.818
Organization trial,

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:26.786
which happened last year.

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:27.420
He did allow

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.122
still photography in the room

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.357
when Allen Weisselberg was sentenced.

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:32.525
But that's just a still photo.

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:33.826
That's not a live feed.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.128
Trump's chief financial officer

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.462
who is serving the final days

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.630
of his prison term.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.132
Jeff,
we just heard from Jason Miller,

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:41.134
who is a campaign adviser to Trump.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.468
He is on the plane with him right now

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.503
on the way here to New York.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.204
He is now saying and of course, we

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:46.372
you know, this is what he is saying.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:47.874
It's not from an FCC filing

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.709
that they've raised $7 million

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.177
since the word of the indictment

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.712
came down on Thursday.

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:53.112
Initially,

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.280
we were told $4 million

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.515
in about 24 hours.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:56.249
And so

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:57.784
we do know that right now

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:59.252
they're saying Trump's not going to speak

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.153
while he's here in New York.

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:00.920
We don't actually know

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:01.921
if that's what's going to happen.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:02.522
What we do know,

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.723
he is planning to speak tomorrow

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:04.924
night back in Mar a Lago.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:07.193
He is he's going to be delivering

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:08.428
an address in primetime

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:08.761
from Mar

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:09.962
a Lago once he returns there

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.998
and really to do it on his own terms.

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:14.700
So it's seen in a way as doing,

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.768
you know, his rebuttal of this.

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:17.236
And his speech will surely go longer

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.304
than the 10 minutes

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:19.806
that he's going to be arraigned tomorrow.

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:20.673
So this is a

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.141
he wants something more dignified,

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:22.842
we're told,

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:24.644
something that's not standing outside

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:25.244
of the courthouse.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.979
So, yes, he wants to gain

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.614
politically from this in the short term,

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:29.582
raising money,

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:30.516
getting his rivals

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:32.251
to put a circle behind him.

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:35.154
But he also wants to sort of frame

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.589
this in a way that,

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:37.423
you know, that he can do it

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:38.491
as a former president.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.359
And he's inviting friends and allies

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:41.394
tomorrow, Lago.

